2025-10-11 08:35:50,043 - evaluation_logger_Attraction-25 - INFO - Final Response: Westminster Abbey is a stunning medieval Gothic abbey that has been the site of every coronation from William the Conqueror to Elizabeth II, as well as 17 royal weddings. It is also the final resting place of many royals and other notable figures, including Queen Elizabeth I, Mary, Queen of Scots, Geoffrey Chaucer, Charles Dickens, Sir Isaac Newton, and Charles Darwin. The abbey also contains the tomb of the Unknown Soldier.

During a tour of the abbey, you can marvel at the 700-year-old coronation chair, admire the 16th-century stonework, and see the portraits of modern martyrs. You can also ascend the 52 feet to the Queen's Diamond Jubilee Galleries, where you can discover a 13th-century triforium that has been hidden for centuries. The galleries now tell the secrets of the abbey.

